cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Peregrine in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Peregrine: heterogeneous linear algebra for Python"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "ElDoumani"
    given-names: "Abdalla"
version: "3.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Abdalla-Eldoumani/peregrine"
abstract: >-
  Peregrine is a linear algebra library for Python with AVX2 CPU kernels and a
  CUDA backend behind a zero-copy, NumPy-compatible API, with per-machine
  calibrated routing between the CPU and the GPU.
keywords:
  - linear algebra
  - matrix multiplication
  - AVX2
  - CUDA
  - NumPy
